setup":"The stock rose about 73% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 5 weeks, peaking at $13.64 and pulling back 16% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Jul 15, 2003 it closed at $13.65, its first close above the base high of $13.64. Volume that day was 1.2M shares, 1.56x the prior 10-day average of 793K. It didn't hold. By Jul 18, 2003 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $15.23.","lesson":"This is an example of a shakeout. The breakout failed by the rules, closing below the level three days running, and then the stock recovered and ran. Cutting it was still the right call when it happened. A failed breakout that fixes itself is worth watching for a re-entry, not a reason to ignore the exit."}}